course: dictionary
lesson: 1727
title: A city, and the people in it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A city is a very large town where many people live and work. You can spot a city by its clues: many people, busy roads and tall buildings. «Light pollution, light from cities, hides the Milky Way from most people who live in towns.» The words «light from cities» sit right next to «towns», so cities are the bigger, busier places.
explain: Sometimes «city» means the people, not the place. Read the whole sentence to find out which meaning is used. A quick check is to swap in «town» or «place» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words come in pairs, like «city centre» (UK) and «downtown» (US). They both mean the middle of a big town. Look for phrases like «capital city» or «city hall» as well: the words next to city often tell you what kind of city it is.
fact: A city is a very large town where many people live and work.
fact: «City» can also mean all the people who live in a city.
fact: In some countries, a town gets the special title of city, often because it has a cathedral.
fact: «City centre» (UK) and «downtown» (US) both mean the middle of a busy city.
fact: «Capital city» means the city where a country's government works.
exercise: A city is a very large town where many people live and work. What is a city? | A kind of train | A river with two hills | A small village with one shop | *A very large town where many people live and work
exercise: «Light pollution, light from cities, hides the Milky Way from most people who live in towns.» What do the cities give out that hides the stars? | Rain | Snow | *Light | Smoke from chimneys
exercise: In some countries a city is a town given that special title, often because it has a cathedral. What might a city have? | *A cathedral | Only one house | A volcano | A sea of sand
test: «The coloured paint marks that workers spray on the pavement are a map of that hidden city.» What do the marks show the diggers? | *Where pipes and cables run | The name of the river | Where to buy ice cream | How tall the buildings are
test: Which sentence uses city to mean the people who live there? | Cities have tall buildings and busy roads. | The city stood on a hill above the river. | The city centre has a big bus station. | *The whole city cheered when the team came home.
exam: A legend says Kyi, Shchek, Khoryv and their sister Lybid founded the city, but it is a legend. What does the word legend tell you? | *The story may not be true | The story is about a city hall | The story is a map of the hidden pipes | The story lists all the capital cities
